The pyrolysis plant market is gaining momentum as industries and waste-management operators seek alternatives for processing difficult waste streams. Pyrolysis uses heat in oxygen-limited conditions to convert materials such as discarded tires, waste plastics, oil sludge and biomass into recoverable products, including pyrolysis oil, recovered carbon black or char, syngas and steel.

Commercial demand is influenced by the availability of suitable feedstock, the quality and marketability of recovered products, environmental compliance requirements and the reliability of plant operations. Project developers increasingly evaluate equipment based on total operating costs, processing capacity, maintenance requirements and the availability of technical support.

